  "notes": [
    "These are complete public NIST ACVP-Server JSON sample vector sets at the pinned commit, copied byte-for-byte. No expected values were generated by this project.",
    "The FIPS203 revision targets the final FIPS 203 ML-KEM standard, not the Kyber submission or FIPS 203 initial public draft.",
    "FIPS203-tr1 is a newer ACVP test revision against the same FIPS 203 standard; it adds seed and expanded decapsulation-key input formats.",
    "Each file is a root JSON object, without the ACVP wire-format protocol-version wrapper. Join prompt, expectedResults, and internalProjection using tgId then tcId within each vector set.",
    "prompt.json contains the inputs. expectedResults.json contains the independent reference outputs. internalProjection.json additionally contains reason labels and intermediate inputs useful for coverage analysis.",
    "KeyGen AFT inputs are d,z (32 bytes each); reference outputs are ek,dk. Encapsulation AFT inputs are ek,m (m is 32 bytes); reference outputs are c,k.",
    "Decapsulation VAL inputs are dk,c for expanded keys or d,z,c for seed keys; reference output is k, including implicit rejection. k is always 32 bytes.",
    "Key-check VAL expected testPassed means whether the supplied key is valid; false is a successful negative test, not a failed golden comparison.",
    "For invalid ciphertexts, the reference output k was independently checked as SHAKE256(z || c, 32 bytes), using the last 32 bytes of dk as z. The internalProjection reason is modified ciphertext.",
    "Local vector agreement is a functional correctness check and does not itself constitute NIST CAVP/CMVP certification or establish constant-time execution or entropy quality."
  ],
